med annoyed: \"Oh, I assure you there's nothing to worry about! Miss Percy, I really didn't say that. I believe the teachers left at 5:00.\" [516] \"Mr. Rowley, was the glass broken at 5:30?\" [517] The young man stared at her. \"Miss Holmes! I really don't know. Are you a detective?\" [518] \"Boy, don't try to play games with me,\" the sergeant said as he approached, but he didn't sound angry and seemed to regain his sense of humor. \"How could that happen?\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 8:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:09 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[1] Prologue\n[2] Joseph's Beard\n[3] The beard was peculiar, strange, even a bit comical, shaped like a French spade, slightly curled, hanging down from the chin, hiding the edges of the collar. The perfect little curls of the beard had a feminine touch, appearing noble, like the splendid beard of Zeus. But what was most captivating was not the wavy rhythm of the long beard; what was truly breathtaking was the color of the beard. [4] This was undeniably Joseph's (1) beard, multicolored, with stripes crisscrossing each other, resembling his robe, shimmering with surprising black, blue, and green. Was the beard colored by the mischievous sun? Or did the wearer of the beard have a hidden agenda, removing the long beard and placing it on the table in the laboratory, dyeing it with a pot of chemicals? This beard that only a god could own, might have an equally astonishing origin. It seemed to be a historically significant beard that should belong to a museum, preserved for future generations to admire. [5] Sam, a retired New York police lieutenant, now runs a private detective agency to soothe his restless spirit. After forty years of police work, he has developed an immunity to human astonishment. But this time, he was startled and then fascinated: on a warm Monday morning in May, the visitor's beard was truly extraordinary and provoked many thoughts. In his past experiences, the lieutenant had never seen such a combination of brilliant colors. He kept opening his eyes wide, as if he could never get enough of it. [6] He finally said, \"Please sit down.\" His voice was weak, and he glanced at the calendar, wondering if he had been bewitched and forgotten it was April Fool's Day. Then, leaning back in his chair, he scratched his stubbly chin, looking at the visitor with a mixture of surprise and awe. [7] The Rainbow Beard sat down nonchalantly. [8] Sam the lieutenant scrutinized him, noting that he was tall and thin, wrapped up like a mummy, as mysterious as his chin. He was dressed in many layers of clothing, looking like his body was wrapped in layers of thick cloth. The lieutenant's trained eyes caught a glimpse of the man's thin wrist above the gloves, and his slender legs \u2013 evidence that he was indeed a thin man. Blue glasses obscured his eyes. He appeared indifferent; the bizarre hat he wore did not come off as he entered the lieutenant's office, hiding his head shape and hair color. [9] He fell into a gloomy silence, reminiscent of Zeus. [10] Sam coughed and encouraged, \"What can I do for you?\" [11] The man with the mustache moved, seeming to perk up. [12] \"Ah, what can I do for you?\" He asked. [13] His two thin legs suddenly crossed, and his gloved hands clasped together on his knees. \"I guess you are Inspector Sam, right?\" The man's voice was slightly hoarse. Sam shuddered nervously, feeling as if he were listening to a god speak. [14] \"I am,\" the inspector said softly. \"You -\"\n[15] A hand waved, \"It doesn't matter, Inspector. The fact is - how should I put it? - I have an unusual request.\" [16] The inspector thought, You don't say! \u2013 and, shaking off his surprise, rose to his feet. His hand moved lightly to the small switch behind his desk, and a barely audible sound was heard, the gentleman with the multicolored mustache apparently not noticing. [17] \"Usually the person sitting in that chair has a request,\" the inspector said lightly. [18] The tip of the man's tongue showed from the mustache around his lips, as if startled by the strange color of the mustache, and quickly withdrew. \"Inspector, I can say this: I've been looking for you for a long time. The reason I'm attracted to you \u2013 is that you seem to be not a typical private detective.\" [19] \"Customer satisfaction is our policy.\" [20] \"Yes, that's right... um \u2013 are you really a private detective? I mean, Inspector, you're not connected to the police now, are you?\" \u2013 the inspector glared at him \u2013 \"You have to understand, I have to make sure that our transaction remains confidential.\" [21] \"I'm very tight-lipped,\" Sam said, looking displeased, \"not even in front of my best friends - you're worried about that, right! Brother, I'm not the kind of person who would betray a friend, unless it's something unspeakable. Sam Detective Agency doesn't mix with bad guys.\" [22] \"No, no, not that kind of thing,\" the man with the rainbow-colored beard quickly chimed in, \"I assure you it's not that kind of thing. It's just that - well, to put it simply, sergeant.\" [23] \"If it's about your wife and her boyfriend,\" the sergeant glanced at him, \"I'm not interested. We don't run that kind of detective agency.\" [24] \"No, no, sergeant, it's not a family dispute, it has nothing to do with that. It's - uh, simply said,\" the man with the rainbow-colored beard said, his breath blowing the colorful beard on his chin, \"I want you to keep something for me.\" [25] \"Oh,\" Sam changed his tone, \"what are you keeping?\" [26] \"An envelope.\" [27] \"An envelope?\" the detective said impatiently, \"What's in it?\" [28] Rainbow Beard showed unexpected firmness, his lips sealed tight. \"No,\" he said, \"I can't tell you. Is that okay?\" [29] The detective's gray eyes stared at the unusual guest for a few seconds, unable to see through the blue glasses. \"I understand,\" it was clear the detective didn't, \"keeping it safe \u2013 what do you mean?\" [30] \"Keeping it safe until I get it back. Like a client would.\" [31] Sam yawned, \"For God's sake, I'm not a banker. Why don't you go to the bank? That's cheaper anyway.\" [32] Rainbow Beard spoke cautiously, \"Sergeant, I'm afraid you don't understand what I mean. You know that won't work. I have to give it to someone to be kept properly, you know, someone honest.\" [33] \"Heard. Understood. Well, anonymous friend, let's see the thing. Look, take a look!\" [34] For a moment, the guest did not respond, but when he did, he was quick and agile, as if he had made a deliberate decision after careful thought. He fumbled around under his layers of clothing with his gloved hands and, after a while, pulled out a long, thick leather envelope. Sam's eyes lit up, and he reached out, the envelope being handed to him \u2013 reluctantly. [35] It was an ordinary envelope that could be bought in any stationery store. The front and back were clean and unmarked. The envelope was sealed with the original self-adhesive tape, and the visitor had pasted six cheap white paper strips on the flap, in various shapes, to prevent others from opening it, obviously anticipating human nature's weaknesses. [36] \"Great,\" said the inspector. \"Great, and not tacky, huh.\" He seemed to casually feel the envelope, but couldn't feel what was inside. He squinted and asked the quiet guest sitting in front of him, \"What's inside? You can't expect -\"\n[37] Rainbow Beard seemed to smile as his beard twisted upward at the corners of his mouth. \"Inspector, I like your persistence, I really do. It confirms what I've heard about you, you know, your reputation is excellent. Your cautious attitude -\"\n[38] \"That's right,\" Sam said impatiently. \"But what's inside?\" [39] The man - if he was a man, Sam suddenly had a whimsical thought - leaned forward. \"If I tell you -\" he said gruffly, \"Inspector, if I tell you - you have an envelope in your hand that contains a clue to a secret, a very important secret, I dare not tell the whole truth to anyone in the world!\" [40] Sam the inspector blinked. He should have known. The peculiar guest's beard, glasses, layers of clothing, and strange behavior - well, this was clearly a madman who had escaped from the asylum! Clues, secrets, anyone in the world... this guy was a madman. [41] \"Ah\u2014take it easy,\" he said. \"Brother, you don't need to be so excited.\" He quickly reached for the small automatic pistol hidden in his armpit gun bag, the lunatic might be armed! [42] Rainbow Beard let out a loud laugh, startling Sam. \"You think I'm crazy. Sergeant, it's not your fault. I can understand why my words might sound\u2014sound\u2014ridiculous. But I swear to you,\" the strange, hoarse voice became clear and steady, \"what I'm telling you is the truth, without exaggeration. Sergeant, you don't need to draw your gun, I won't bite you.\" [43] Sam withdrew his hand from his coat, flushing red and glaring at the guest. [44] The guest continued triumphantly, \"That's better, really. Now listen carefully, because I don't have time, it's crucial that you understand. I repeat, the envelope contains a clue, Sergeant, a clue to a colossal secret. I'll add one more thing,\" his tone grew serious, \"a secret worth millions!\" [45] \"Hmph, if you're not crazy, then I must be,\" Sam said grumpily. \"You want me to believe your nonsense, you need to tell me more. A secret worth millions\u2014what do you mean? In this flat envelope?\" [46] \"Undoubtedly.\" [47] \"Political secret?\" [48] \"No.\" [49] \"Oil mine? Extortion - love letters? Treasure? Jewels? Come on, brother, be clear. If I don't know what's going on, I won't bother with this.\" [50] \"But I can't tell you.\" Rainbow Beard answered with a hint of impatience, \"Don't be silly, Chief. I swear on my honor that the contents of the envelope are not evil. This secret is quite legitimate and has nothing to do with the mundane things you mentioned earlier; it's much more interesting and valuable. Remember, the envelope contains a clue to the secret, not the secret itself. I'll say it again, the envelope contains a clue to solving the secret.\" [51] Sam exclaimed angrily, \"You're driving me crazy. Why the secrecy? Why should I keep this damn thing?\" [52] \"There's a good reason for it.\" Rainbow Beard pursed his lips, \"I'm following a trail - the 'source' of the clue, the secret I mentioned. You know, I haven't found it yet. But this clue is very important, really important! I believe we can succeed. Alright, if - if something happens to me, Inspector, I want you to open this envelope.\" [53] \"Huh.\" The Inspector grunted. [54] \"If something happens to me - when you open the envelope - you'll see my little clue. It can guide you in a roundabout way to - me, or rather, my fate. Understand, I'm not asking for someone to avenge me. If something happens to me, I'm not interested in revenge; I just want to keep the original secret intact. Is that clear enough?\" [55] \"Damn it!\" [56] The man with the rainbow beard sighed. \"The clue in the envelope is just a clue, nothing more. The clue itself doesn't reveal anything, but that's exactly what I want! This incomplete trait can protect me from\u2014dear Inspector, I mean no offense\u2014your curiosity, or anyone else's curiosity who might open the envelope. If you open it before I ask you to, I assure you there's nothing meaningful in it for you.\" [57] \"Oh, come on!\" The inspector stood up, his face turning purple. \"You're trying to play games with me, you think you're scaring someone with this kid's trick? Get out of here. I can't waste\u2014\"\n[58] There was a persistent noise on the inspector's desk, but the guest ignored it. The inspector suppressed his imminent anger and picked up the handset of the intercom phone. A female voice bombarded his ear. He reluctantly listened for a