so I won't tell you my name or anything else! Because if nothing happens - I can't think of what could happen - I don't want anyone else to have a clear lead to inquire about my secret. I believe that's clear enough, sergeant...\"\n[67] \"Good God,\" the sergeant grumbled, \"is that too much? Listen, you're mistaken. I thought you were crazy at first, and now I don't know what to think, but listen: if you leave this place immediately, I'll feel better. Go! Out!\" [68] The visitor's confusion was evident on his face. The phone rang again. Sam jumped up, his face flushed with embarrassment, as if a boy caught stealing an apple, his fists stuffed into his pockets. \"Alright, alright.\" He stammered into the phone and then loudly put it down, \"I'm sorry. I - I woke up in a bad mood this morning. I don't think I'm used to this kind of -\"\n[69] The visitor breathed a sigh of relief. \"I'm so glad - ah. Very clever, sergeant, really very clever. I hadn't thought of that. \" He chuckled, rubbing his hands together, \"Really, it's quite exhilarating. Like the mad adventures of Robin Hood.\" [70] \"Whose?\" Sam asked curiously. [71] \"Notorious Arsen\u00e8 Lupin (2). Ah, a code! A code, of course! When I called you, I should have said\u2014let me think\u2014Ha! 'I'm from outer space. A million!' I said, and you would have known it was me. Ha, ha!\" [72] \"Ha, ha,\" the detective said. \"\u2018I'm from\u2014'\u201d He cautiously shook his head, and a glimmer of hope shone in his eyes. \"But, my fee\u2014\u201d\n[73] \"Ah, your fee,\" the man with the rainbow-colored mustache said. \"Yes, yes, I almost forgot. Detective, what is your fee for taking on this strange little case?\" [74] \"Just for putting that annoying envelope in my safe?\" [75] \"That's right.\" [76] \"That would cost you -\" The sergeant said urgently, \"Just five hundred jingles.\" [77] \"Jingles?\" Rainbow Beard repeated, obviously confused. [78] \"Iron Man, dollars, money! Five hundred dollars!\" Sam shouted. He eagerly searched the customer's face for signs of difficulty: the chin that should have dropped under the terrible beard should have dropped, he hoped, so that the outrageous demand would scare off the visitor and he could breathe a sigh of relief without losing face. [79] \"Oh.\" The client smiled slightly, not at all surprised. He reached into his loose-fitting clothes and pulled out a thick wallet, withdrawing a crisp bill and dropping it onto the table. [80] It was a brand new thousand-dollar bill. [81] \"I think,\" Rainbow Beard said lightly, \"that a thousand yuan is a reasonable price. This is an unusual, and \u2013 ah \u2013 unconventional case, and besides, it's worth it for me. It brings a sense of security \u2013\"\n[82] \"Um \u2013 uh.\" Sam swallowed and touched the bill with his fingers, astonished. [83] \"It's settled then,\" the client said, getting up. \"There are two more conditions, officer. I require you to strictly adhere to them. First, you cannot \u2013 how did you put it? \u2013 have someone follow me when I leave the office; and second, you cannot contact me unless I haven't called you on a certain twenty-day day.\" [84] \"Of course, of course.\" Sam said in a trembling voice. A thousand yuan! Tears of joy welled up in his flinty eyes. These days business had been so slow! To lock a flat envelope in the safe and receive a thousand yuan! [85] \"Second \u2013\" the visitor said lightly, heading towards the door, \"if I haven't called you on a certain twenty-day day, you cannot open the envelope \u2013 unless in the presence of Mr. Philo Vance.\" [86] The inspector's mouth gaped like a bat hole, and this last blow was a knockout. The Rainbow Beard sneered and strode out, disappearing. [87] Perkins Sam, female, over twenty-one years old, straightforward, fair-skinned, with golden hair. From a gardening perspective, she was her father's apple, the saying goes, the apple of his eye. She quickly pulled off her headphones and neatly placed them in the bottom drawer of her desk in the front hall. This drawer was used to receive the conversations from the wiretaps installed in her father's modern office. The door opened, and the tall, blue-eyed, blue-bearded stranger appeared, seemingly unaware of Perkins.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 9:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:09 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[1715] The inspector strode back, barking, \"Vera!\" \u2013 the thief immediately tensed \u2013 \"My good child, come with me!\" [1716] \"You want - you want to take me where?\" [1717] \"You'll find out soon enough.\" - the scholars had stopped talking and were looking anxiously and seriously at Inspector Sam - \"Dr. Sedra, are you staying here?\" [1718] \"What did you say?\" the Briton whispered, surprised. [1719] \"We're going to check out Dr. Aless's den.\" The inspector grinned slyly. \"Maybe you'd like to come along too.\" [1720] \"Hey -\" Vera swallowed. [1721] Dr. Sedra frowned. \"I'm afraid I don't understand your meaning.\" [1722] \"I have many things to discuss with Dr. Sedra today,\" Dr. Jott impatiently said. [1723] \"Ah, so,\" Reine suddenly stood up, \"Officer, forget it. Dr. Sedra must not be fond of American enthusiasm after this terrible incident. And, Dr., where do you live? In case we need to find you urgently \u2014\"\n[1724] \"The Seneca Hotel, Mr. Reine.\" [1725] \"Thank you. Let's go, Officer. Percy, Gordon, it seems we can't get rid of you.\" The old gentleman chuckled, \"Ah, curious young people.\" He shook his head thoughtfully and headed towards the door. [1726] Chapter 19\n[1727] The Mysterious House\n[1728] With the reluctant Italian leading the way, Dromio drives the Lincoln away from the main road and into a narrow path between the towns of Ephesus and Tirrano. This little road is made of gravel, with low-hanging branches on both sides. They suddenly emerge from the dull 